      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISCHIEF AFOOT (1) was safely held last time out, finishing eighth at The Gardens over 400m behind Camaro Rose (24.03) in a Grade 5. Was in the money prior to that. Form from her last run is proving strong. Tough to beat if on-song. REDEEM A ARCADIA (7) showed blistering pace early and gave a sight when in the minors, beaten 2.75 lengths over 300m this track in 17.59. Leading player again. MULWEE HARRY (8) is mixing form lately, finishing out of the placings last time at this track but was a Maiden winner two back at this track. Well placed here and should do much better. MISDIRECTION (6) won by a wide margin last start. Sure to run well again. Something for the Multiples: KICKER MINI (5) BARRELLED (3)",
